# Migrating Flat Pulumi Program to ComponentResource with Aliases

This guide shows how to refactor your flat TypeScript Pulumi program to use `ComponentResource` without replacing existing resources. The key is using **aliases** to map old URNs to new logical hierarchies.

## Migration Strategy

1. **Phase 1**: Create the ComponentResource class with alias mappings
2. **Phase 2**: Update the main stack file to instantiate the component
3. **Phase 3**: Deploy with `--refresh=false` to preserve state

## Step 1: Create the ComponentResource

Create `components/infrastructure.ts`:

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";

interface InfraConfig {
  environment: "dev" | "prod";
  nodeCount: number;
  nodeType: string;
  dbInstanceClass: string;
  dbMultiAz: boolean;
  enableReplication: boolean;
}

export class WebAppInfrastructure extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
  public cluster: eks.Cluster;
  public bucket: aws.s3.Bucket;
  public database: aws.rds.Instance;
  public serviceRole: aws.iam.Role;
  public dbSecret: aws.secretsmanager.Secret;

  constructor(
    name: string,
    config: InfraConfig,
    opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions
  ) {
    super("custom:infrastructure:WebAppInfrastructure", name, {}, opts);

    const env = config.environment;

    // ===== EKS Cluster =====
    this.cluster = new eks.Cluster(
      `${env}-cluster`,
      {
        version: "1.28",
        roleArn: this.createClusterRole().arn,
        vpcConfig: {
          subnetIds: this.createSubnets().map((s) => s.id),
        },
        enableLogging: {
          apiServer: true,
          audit: true,
          authenticator: true,
          controllerManager: true,
          scheduler: true,
        },
        managedNodeGroups: [
          {
            name: `${env}-nodes`,
            desiredCapacity: config.nodeCount,
            minSize: config.nodeCount,
            maxSize: config.nodeCount + 2,
            instanceTypes: [config.nodeType],
            labels: { Environment: env },
          },
        ],
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [
        // Map old flat resource URN to new hierarchical one
        new pulumi.URN("pulumi", pulumi.getStack(), "aws:eks/cluster:Cluster", `${env}-cluster`, "")
      ]}
    );

    // ===== S3 Bucket for Assets =====
    this.bucket = new aws.s3.Bucket(
      `${env}-assets`,
      {
        acl: "private",
        versioning: { enabled: true },
        serverSideEncryptionConfiguration: {
          rule: {
            applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: {
              sseAlgorithm: "AES256",
            },
          },
        },
        objectLockConfiguration: {
          objectLockEnabled: "Enabled",
        },
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [
        // Old flat URN
        { name: `${env}-assets` }
      ]}
    );

    // Block all public access to bucket
    new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock(
      `${env}-assets-pab`,
      {
        bucket: this.bucket.id,
        blockPublicAcls: true,
        blockPublicPolicy: true,
        ignorePublicAcls: true,
        restrictPublicBuckets: true,
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // Replication for prod
    if (config.enableReplication) {
      const replicationRole = new aws.iam.Role(
        `${env}-replication-role`,
        {
          assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
              {
                Effect: "Allow",
                Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" },
                Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
              },
            ],
          }),
        },
        { parent: this }
      );

      new aws.iam.RolePolicy(
        `${env}-replication-policy`,
        {
          role: replicationRole.id,
          policy: pulumi.output(this.bucket.arn).apply((arn) =>
            JSON.stringify({
              Version: "2012-10-17",
              Statement: [
                {
                  Effect: "Allow",
                  Action: ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"],
                  Resource: arn,
                },
                {
                  Effect: "Allow",
                  Action: ["s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication"],
                  Resource: `${arn}/*`,
                },
              ],
            })
          ),
        },
        { parent: this }
      );

      new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfiguration(
        `${env}-replication`,
        {
          bucket: this.bucket.id,
          role: replicationRole.arn,
          rules: [
            {
              status: "Enabled",
              priority: 1,
              filter: { prefix: "" },
              destination: {
                bucket: `arn:aws:s3:::${env}-assets-replica`,
                replicationTime: {
                  status: "Enabled",
                  time: 15,
                },
              },
            },
          ],
        },
        { parent: this }
      );
    }

    // ===== RDS Instance =====
    const dbSubnetGroup = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup(
      `${env}-db-subnet`,
      {
        subnetIds: this.createSubnets().map((s) => s.id),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    const dbSecurityGroup = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup(
      `${env}-db-sg`,
      {
        vpcId: this.createVpc().id,
        ingress: [
          {
            protocol: "tcp",
            fromPort: 5432,
            toPort: 5432,
            securityGroups: [this.createAppSecurityGroup().id],
          },
        ],
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    this.database = new aws.rds.Instance(
      `${env}-postgres`,
      {
        identifier: `${env}-postgres`,
        engine: "postgres",
        engineVersion: "15.3",
        instanceClass: config.dbInstanceClass,
        allocatedStorage: 20,
        dbName: "appdb",
        username: "postgres",
        passwordSecretRef: {
          name: "db-password", // from secrets manager
        },
        dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnetGroup.name,
        vpcSecurityGroupIds: [dbSecurityGroup.id],
        multiAz: config.dbMultiAz,
        storageEncrypted: true,
        kmsKeyId: this.createKmsKey().arn,
        backupRetentionPeriod: 7,
        backupWindow: "03:00-04:00",
        skipFinalSnapshot: env === "dev",
        finalSnapshotIdentifier: env === "prod" ? `${env}-postgres-final` : undefined,
        deletionProtection: env === "prod",
        publiclyAccessible: false,
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [
        { name: `${env}-postgres` }
      ]}
    );

    // ===== Service Role & Inline Policy =====
    this.serviceRole = new aws.iam.Role(
      `${env}-service-role`,
      {
        assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
          Version: "2012-10-17",
          Statement: [
            {
              Effect: "Allow",
              Principal: {
                AWS: this.cluster.core.oidcProvider.arn,
              },
              Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
              Condition: {
                StringEquals: {
                  [`${this.cluster.core.oidcProvider.url}:sub`]:
                    "system:serviceaccount:default:app",
                },
              },
            },
          ],
        }),
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [
        { name: `${env}-service-role` }
      ]}
    );

    // Least-privilege policy for prod; broader for dev
    const policyDocument =
      env === "prod"
        ? {
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
              {
                Effect: "Allow",
                Action: ["s3:GetObject"],
                Resource: `${this.bucket.arn}/*`,
              },
              {
                Effect: "Allow",
                Action: ["secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"],
                Resource: `arn:aws:secretsmanager:*:*:secret:${env}-db-*`,
              },
            ],
          }
        : {
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
              {
                Effect: "Allow",
                Action: ["s3:*"],
                Resource: `${this.bucket.arn}/*`,
              },
              {
                Effect: "Allow",
                Action: ["secretsmanager:*"],
                Resource: `arn:aws:secretsmanager:*:*:secret:*`,
              },
            ],
          };

    new aws.iam.RolePolicy(
      `${env}-service-policy`,
      {
        role: this.serviceRole.id,
        policy: JSON.stringify(policyDocument),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // ===== Secrets Manager Secret (DB Connection) =====
    this.dbSecret = new aws.secretsmanager.Secret(
      `${env}-db-connection`,
      {
        name: `${env}-db-connection-string`,
        description: "Database connection string",
      },
      { parent: this, aliases: [
        { name: `${env}-db-connection` }
      ]}
    );

    new aws.secretsmanager.SecretVersion(
      `${env}-db-connection-version`,
      {
        secretId: this.dbSecret.id,
        secretString: pulumi.secret(
          this.database.endpoint.apply(
            (endpoint) =>
              `postgresql://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@${endpoint}:5432/appdb`
          )
        ),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );

    // ===== CloudFront (prod) or ALB (dev) =====
    if (env === "prod") {
      this.createCloudFront();
    } else {
      this.createAlb();
    }

    this.registerOutputs({
      clusterName: this.cluster.eksCluster.name,
      bucketName: this.bucket.id,
      databaseEndpoint: this.database.endpoint,
      serviceRoleArn: this.serviceRole.arn,
      secretArn: this.dbSecret.arn,
    });
  }

  private createClusterRole(): aws.iam.Role {
    return new aws.iam.Role("eks-cluster-role", {
      assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
        Version: "2012-10-17",
        Statement: [
          {
            Effect: "Allow",
            Principal: { Service: "eks.amazonaws.com" },
            Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
          },
        ],
      }),
    });
  }

  private createVpc(): aws.ec2.Vpc {
    return new aws.ec2.Vpc(`${this.name}-vpc`, {
      cidrBlock: "10.0.0.0/16",
      enableDnsHostnames: true,
      enableDnsSupport: true,
    });
  }

  private createSubnets(): aws.ec2.Subnet[] {
    const vpc = this.createVpc();
    return [
      new aws.ec2.Subnet(`${this.name}-subnet-1`, {
        vpcId: vpc.id,
        cidrBlock: "10.0.1.0/24",
        availabilityZone: "us-east-1a",
      }),
      new aws.ec2.Subnet(`${this.name}-subnet-2`, {
        vpcId: vpc.id,
        cidrBlock: "10.0.2.0/24",
        availabilityZone: "us-east-1b",
      }),
    ];
  }

  private createAppSecurityGroup(): aws.ec2.SecurityGroup {
    return new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup(`${this.name}-app-sg`, {
      vpcId: this.createVpc().id,
      egress: [
        {
          protocol: "-1",
          fromPort: 0,
          toPort: 0,
          cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"],
        },
      ],
    });
  }

  private createKmsKey(): aws.kms.Key {
    return new aws.kms.Key(`${this.name}-key`, {
      description: "KMS key for RDS encryption",
      deletionWindowInDays: 7,
    });
  }

  private createCloudFront(): aws.cloudfront.Distribution {
    const acmCert = new aws.acm.Certificate(`prod-cert`, {
      domainName: "example.com",
      validationMethod: "DNS",
    });

    return new aws.cloudfront.Distribution(
      "prod-cdn",
      {
        enabled: true,
        isIpv6Enabled: true,
        defaultCacheBehavior: {
          allowedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
          cachedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
          targetOriginId: this.bucket.id,
          viewerProtocolPolicy: "https-only",
          forwardedValues: {
            queryString: false,
            cookies: { forward: "none" },
          },
        },
        origins: [
          {
            domainName: this.bucket.bucketRegionalDomainName,
            originId: this.bucket.id,
            s3OriginConfig: {
              originAccessIdentity: new aws.cloudfront.OriginAccessIdentity(
                "prod-oai"
              ).cloudfrontAccessIdentityPath,
            },
          },
        ],
        restrictions: {
          geoRestriction: { restrictionType: "none" },
        },
        viewerCertificate: {
          acmCertificateArn: acmCert.arn,
          sslSupportMethod: "sni-only",
        },
      },
      { parent: this }
    );
  }

  private createAlb(): aws.lb.LoadBalancer {
    return new aws.lb.LoadBalancer(
      "dev-alb",
      {
        internal: true,
        loadBalancerType: "application",
        subnets: this.createSubnets().map((s) => s.id),
      },
      { parent: this }
    );
  }
}
```

## Step 2: Update Main Stack File

Replace your flat `index.ts` with:

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { WebAppInfrastructure } from "./components/infrastructure";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const env = pulumi.getStack(); // "dev" or "prod"

if (env !== "dev" && env !== "prod") {
  throw new Error("Stack must be 'dev' or 'prod'");
}

const infra = new WebAppInfrastructure(`webapp-${env}`, {
  environment: env,
  nodeCount: env === "dev" ? 2 : 4,
  nodeType: env === "dev" ? "t3.medium" : "t3.large",
  dbInstanceClass: env === "dev" ? "db.t3.micro" : "db.t3.medium",
  dbMultiAz: env === "prod",
  enableReplication: env === "prod",
});

// Export key values for downstream use
export const clusterName = infra.cluster.eksCluster.name;
export const bucketName = infra.bucket.id;
export const databaseEndpoint = infra.database.endpoint;
export const serviceRoleArn = infra.serviceRole.arn;
```

## Step 3: Stack Configuration

Create `Pulumi.dev.yaml`:
```yaml
name: myapp
runtime: typescript
description: Web app infrastructure (dev)
```

Create `Pulumi.prod.yaml`:
```yaml
name: myapp
runtime: typescript
description: Web app infrastructure (prod)
```

## Step 4: Deployment

**Before deploying**, understand the alias mapping:

- Old URN: `urn:pulumi:dev::myapp::aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::dev-assets`
- New URN: `urn:pulumi:dev::myapp::custom:infrastructure:WebAppInfrastructure$aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::dev-assets`

The `aliases` parameter in ComponentResource tells Pulumi to treat the new hierarchical resource as an update to the old flat one.

**Deploy safely:**

```bash
# Preview without making changes
pulumi preview --stack dev

# If satisfied, deploy with state migration
# (no --refresh flag needed; aliases handle the rename)
pulumi up --stack dev

# Repeat for prod
pulumi up --stack prod
```

## Key Points

1. **Aliases use a simple name mapping** (`{ name: "old-name" }`) or full URN references
2. **Parent relationship (`parent: this`)** automatically qualifies the new URN
3. **Deployment order matters**: update one stack at a time to verify behavior
4. **No data loss**: aliases preserve stack state; S3 buckets, databases, and secrets remain unchanged
5. **Environment configs** (`dev.yaml`, `prod.yaml`) keep parameters isolated per stack

This approach maintains full backward compatibility while enabling cleaner, reusable infrastructure code.
